{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"","sections":{"preamble":"You are a coding assistant running inside pi, a coding agent harness. Help users inspect files, run commands, and modify code.","tools":"<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n\nAdditional tools may be available.\n</tools>","rules":"<rules>\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\n- Use edit for targeted changes. Batch changes to one file in a single call.\n- Each edits[].oldText must exactly and uniquely match the original file. Keep matches short and non-overlapping; merge nearby changes without including large unchanged regions.\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\n- Be concise in your responses\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\n</rules>","docs":"<docs>\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about the harness itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\n- Main documentation: /Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/install/releases/1.5.0/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/README.md\n- Additional docs: /Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/install/releases/1.5.0/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs\n- Examples: /Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/install/releases/1.5.0/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\n- Before implementing harness changes, read the relevant docs and examples in full, following related cross-references.\n</docs>","addendum":"<addendum>\nFirst, call bash exactly once with command `printf 'first tool done\\n'`; wait for it to finish. Then answer in one short sentence. Do not use any other tools.\n\n</addendum>","project_context":"<project_context>\nProject-specific instructions and guidelines:\n\n<project_instructions path=\"/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/AGENTS.md\">\n# Global agent notes\n\n## Wiki\n\nFor fiber and switchyard work, the team's memory is the wiki at `~/work/wiki`. Before a decision, read its `index.md`. Add durable findings as pages, following `CONVENTIONS.md`. A role restarting reads `state/<role>.md` first.\n\n## When to delegate\n\nDelegate plan writing from an approved spec, well-scoped coding, review, and bulk reading,\ntriage or summarising. Keep the product decision, and any edit the owner wants to watch, for\nyourself.\n\nThe verify loop decides, not the size of the edit. An edit that needs a test or build run to\nverify goes to another agent with that check as its gate, however small: a three-line change can\nstart a run-and-fix loop that fills this session's context. A small edit to docs or config that\nneeds no verify loop stays in the session.\n\n## How to delegate\n\nThe delegate skill holds the model tiers, the pick rule and the two authority lines a brief\ncarries. The tool depends on the model's provider:\n\n- **`opencode-go/*` and `openai-codex/*`:** `subagent_spawn`. A tier entry's `:<level>` suffix\n  goes in `thinking`, so `openai-codex/gpt-6-luna:xhigh` is model `openai-codex/gpt-6-luna`\n  with thinking `xhigh`; without a suffix, use `medium`. The result arrives as a notice, so\n  there is nothing to wait on.\n- **cursor (`composer-2.5`, `grok-*`) and Claude (`claude-*`):** `delegate run`. Wait with\n  `bash` and `run_in_background: true` on `delegate watch <ids>`: one notice arrives when every\n  job is terminal.\n\n</project_instructions>\n</project_context>","skills":"<skills>\nThe following skills provide specialized instructions for specific tasks.\nUse the read tool to load a skill's file when the task matches its description.\nResolve relative paths against the skill's directory (parent of SKILL.md). Use absolute paths in tool calls.\n\n<available_skills>\n  <skill>\n    <name>attack-the-premise</name>\n    <description>My second fix failed the same test, gate or review finding as the first. Use before starting a third patch: stop patching, write down the assumption both fixes share, and question it.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/attack-the-premise/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>autonomous-flywheel</name>\n    <description>Flywheel: land a stack of tickets or PRs through parallel lanes, at any hour, with the owner away: frontier, fences, merge terms, round report. Fires when asked to run or continue a flywheel session, or to land a stack of PRs.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/autonomous-flywheel/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>ci-triage</name>\n    <description>Classify a failed CI run before any retry or fix: real failure, flake, stale base, merge conflict or infrastructure. Use when CI fails on a PR, or before rerunning any CI job.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/ci-triage/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>clear-communication</name>\n    <description>Write and edit prose in GOV.UK / GDS style — plain English, active voice, front-loaded, sentence case, no bold/italic emphasis. Use when writing or editing reports, research write-ups, guidance, documentation, summaries, or any prose where clarity and accessibility matter.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/clear-communication/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>code-review</name>\n    <description>Review the changes since a fixed point (commit, branch, tag, or merge-base) on two axes: Standards (does the code follow this repo&apos;s documented standards?) and Spec (does it do what the issue or spec asked, and nothing else?). Ends in one verdict per axis. Use when asked to review a branch, a PR or work in progress, to review since X, or to verify a repair against earlier findings.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/code-review/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>codebase-design</name>\n    <description>Shared vocabulary for designing deep modules. Use when the user wants to design or improve a module&apos;s interface, find deepening opportunities, decide where a seam goes, make code more testable or AI-navigable, or when another skill needs the deep-module vocabulary.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/codebase-design/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>debt-ledger</name>\n    <description>Harvest every `debt:` comment into a ledger of deliberate shortcuts, flagging any with no upgrade trigger or that weaken a stated rule. Use when asked what was deferred, which shortcuts were taken, or for the debt ledger. Reports only.\n</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/debt-ledger/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>delegate</name>\n    <description>Run work on other models through the `delegate` CLI. Use when starting a delegated job, picking a model, writing a brief, waiting on or reading a job, or answering a NEEDS_CONTEXT job with resume.\n</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/delegate/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>diagnosing-bugs</name>\n    <description>Diagnosis loop for hard bugs and performance regressions. Use when the user says &quot;diagnose&quot;/&quot;debug this&quot;, or reports something broken/throwing/failing/slow.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/diagnosing-bugs/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>domain-modeling</name>\n    <description>Build and sharpen a project&apos;s domain model. Use when discussing codebase terminology, writing or editing a GLOSSARY.md, or recording or editing an ADR.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/domain-modeling/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>goal-sloc</name>\n    <description>Playbook for using lines-of-code (SLOC) as a north-star metric to genuinely simplify and improve an engineering solution — without gaming the number. Use when asked to &quot;cut SLOC&quot;, &quot;reduce/simplify the codebase&quot;, remove bloat/complexity/tech-debt, delete dead code or duplication, or hit a line-count target. Covers preflight (baseline + feedback loops + tooling), an honest reduction order, a self-audit against gaming, stop conditions, and a Flutter reference.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/goal-sloc/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>grill-with-docs</name>\n    <description>Grill a plan or design and record what it settles as ADRs and a glossary. Use when a decision must be both stress-tested and written down; use grilling alone when the interview needs no lasting record.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/grill-with-docs/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>grilling</name>\n    <description>Grill the user relentlessly about a plan, decision, or idea. Use when the user wants to stress-test their thinking, or uses any &apos;grill&apos; trigger phrases.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/grilling/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>handoff</name>\n    <description>Compact the current conversation into a handoff document for another agent to pick up.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/handoff/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>herdr-automations</name>\n    <description>Write Sheprd automations: small Luau scripts that run on a schedule or by hand to pull a branch, run validation or commands, start agents in new worktrees with a prompt, and notify. Use it inside Herdr (HERDR_ENV=1) when the user asks for something to happen every day, every few hours, at a time, on a cron schedule, or on demand with one command: a nightly or recurring job, a scheduled agent, an automation, a routine, or &apos;every morning do X&apos;. It covers writing the script, checking its plan with /Applications/Herdr.app/Contents/MacOS/sheprd-automate check, and asking the user to approve it; never approve it yourself.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/herdr-automations/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>herdr-gpui-browser</name>\n    <description>Open a browser tab in Sheprd beside your terminal to show the user a web page, HTML file, or mockup, and get back their notes and picks. Use it inside Herdr (HERDR_ENV=1) when the user asks to open, start, or show a browser tab, page, preview, or mockup, to explain, demo, or visualize how something works, or to mock up UI variants to pick from; prefer it there over other browser skills, a system browser, or long text explanations. Also use it for what Sheprd, not the herdr daemon, shows or keeps: a file at a line, a review of your changes, worktree notes, checkpoints and their diffs, your branch&apos;s pull request and CI, vulnerability reports and Dependabot alerts, asking the user to approve an automation script you wrote, forwarding, opening, or stopping ports, creating, running commands on, or deleting cloud machines, remote control from a phone, listing or focusing the app&apos;s windows and tabs, waiting for a tab to close or the user&apos;s notes, Sheprd settings, themes, and fonts, and keeping the machine awake.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/herdr-gpui-browser/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>herdr-mods</name>\n    <description>Write Sheprd mods: small sandboxed Luau extensions that add a status bar item, a sidebar section, a section of the right-hand mod panel, palette commands, or an app with its own activity bar icon to Sheprd without changing its code, reloaded live when saved. Use it inside Herdr (HERDR_ENV=1) when the user asks to extend, customize, or add to Sheprd&apos;s own interface: show a count, a list, a meter, or a button in the status bar, the sidebar, or a panel beside the terminals (like opencode&apos;s sidebar), add a palette command, add an activity bar app such as a dashboard of agents or workspaces, or write a mod, plugin, extension, or widget for Sheprd. It covers the folder layout, the element tree, checking a mod with /Applications/Herdr.app/Contents/MacOS/sheprd mod check, and reading its errors and logs.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/herdr-mods/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>implement</name>\n    <description>Take one ticket from start to merge: preflight, plan, Verifier, lane, gate, review, CI, merge. Use when asked to implement, land or work a ticket end to end, in session or as a sub-orchestrator.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/implement/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>improve-codebase-architecture</name>\n    <description>Scan a codebase for deepening opportunities, present them as a visual HTML report, then grill through whichever one you pick.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/improve-codebase-architecture/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>overbuild-audit</name>\n    <description>Whole-repo audit for over-engineering: a ranked list of what to delete, simplify, or replace with stdlib or native equivalents. Use when the user asks to audit a codebase for bloat or what can be deleted from a repo. Reports only; applies nothing.\n</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/overbuild-audit/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>overbuild-review</name>\n    <description>Over-engineering review of a diff: what to delete, or replace with stdlib or a native feature. Use when asked to review for over-engineering, or what a change could cut. Reports only; applies nothing.\n</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/overbuild-review/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>planning</name>\n    <description>Write a ticket&apos;s implementation plan: a contract sketch (rulings, files, tasks, interfaces, review focus), checked by a Verifier, posted on the ticket, and filled into the lane brief. Use when planning a ticket before a lane builds it, or filling a preflight, planner, Verifier or lane brief.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/planning/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>prototype</name>\n    <description>Build a throwaway prototype to answer a design question. Use when the user wants to sanity-check whether a state model or logic feels right, or explore what a UI should look like.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/prototype/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>quota</name>\n    <description>Quota left on the AI subscriptions (Claude, Codex, Cursor, OpenCode Go, Muse), read live from QuotaBar. Use when asked how much quota remains or when it resets, or when a pick rule needs headroom.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/quota/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>research</name>\n    <description>Investigate a question against high-trust primary sources and capture the findings as a Markdown file in the repo. Use when the user wants a topic researched, docs or API facts gathered, or reading legwork delegated to a background agent.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/research/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>resolving-merge-conflicts</name>\n    <description>Use when you need to resolve an in-progress git merge/rebase conflict.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/resolving-merge-conflicts/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>retro</name>\n    <description>Conduct a retrospective on a coding session or a flywheel round, and file the durable lessons. Use when asked for a retro, or when a flywheel round closes.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/retro/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>review-loop</name>\n    <description>Review, repair and verify a PR until it can merge: reviews from a different model family, fix rounds with scoped verifies, and a two-round stop. Use when a PR needs review before merge, whether it came from implement, the flywheel&apos;s PR-stack mode, or triage.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/review-loop/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>rex</name>\n    <description>Use the rex CLI to manage Rex sessions, open tabs, arrange panes, run commands, inspect terminal output, and control connected Rex apps.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/rex/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>setup-agent-skills</name>\n    <description>Set up a repo for the agent skills: issue tracker, triage labels, glossary layout and workflow doc. Use when a skill reports &quot;repo not set up&quot;. It interviews the owner, so only the main orchestrator runs it, with the owner present.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/setup-agent-skills/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>tdd</name>\n    <description>Test-driven development. Use when the user wants to build features or fix bugs test-first, mentions &quot;red-green-refactor&quot;, or wants integration tests.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/tdd/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>to-spec</name>\n    <description>Turn the current conversation into a spec and publish it to the project issue tracker: no interview, just synthesis of what you&apos;ve already discussed.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/to-spec/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>to-tickets</name>\n    <description>Break a plan, spec, or the current conversation into a set of tracer-bullet tickets, each declaring its blocking edges, published to the configured tracker (edges as text in one file per ticket locally, or native blocking links on a real tracker).</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/to-tickets/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>triage</name>\n    <description>Move issues and external PRs through a state machine of triage roles, categorise, verify, grill if needed, and write agent-ready briefs.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/triage/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>wait-what</name>\n    <description>Re-pitch a message that did not land, in plain language grounded in the repo&apos;s vocabulary. Use when the user says they are lost or confused, asks what you just said, or pushes back on too much text or jargon.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/wait-what/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>wayfinder</name>\n    <description>Plan a huge chunk of work (more than one agent session can hold) as a shared map of decision tickets on your issue tracker, and resolve them one at a time until the way to the destination is clear.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/wayfinder/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>wizard</name>\n    <description>Generate an interactive bash wizard that walks a human through steps only they can perform. Use when provisioning infrastructure, setting up credentials or CI secrets, walking an unfamiliar third-party dashboard, or running a one-off migration or cutover. Don&apos;t invoke this for steps the agent can perform itself.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/wizard/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>writing-for-agents</name>\n    <description>Writing documents for agents. Use when creating or editing skills, or modifying AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md.</description>\n    <location>/Users/aakshintala/.pi/agent/skills/writing-for-agents/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n</available_skills>\n</skills>","cwd":"<cwd>\n/private/tmp/sy-1581-pi-recording/run9\n</cwd>","ponytail":"<ponytail>\nBuild the simplest thing that works. Read the task and the code it touches first, then take the first rung that holds:\n1. Skip what nobody asked for.\n2. Reuse what this codebase already has.\n3. Use the standard library.\n4. Use a native platform feature.\n5. Use an installed dependency; add a new one only when a few lines won't do.\n6. Only then write the minimum new code.\nFix bugs at the root cause: check every caller, then fix the shared code once.\nKeep, however small the change: validation at trust boundaries, error handling that prevents data loss, security, accessibility, and anything the user asked for.\n</ponytail>"},"timestamp":1794371339525,"toolsAdded":[{"name":"read","description":"Read the contents of a file. Supports text files and images (jpg, png, gif, webp, bmp). Images are sent as attachments. For text files, output is truncated to 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Use offset/limit for large files. When you need the full file, continue with offset until complete.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to read (relative or absolute)"},"offset":{"type":"number","description":"Line number to start reading from (1-indexed)"},"limit":{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of lines to read"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"bash","description":"Run a bash command. Returns its output (the last 2000 lines or 50KB). A command still running after 30s moves to the background: you get its job ID and log path, and a notice when it ends. Set run_in_background for servers and long builds. Read logs with read.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["command"],"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"command":{"type":"string","description":"Bash command"},"timeout":{"type":"number","description":"Seconds, then killed"},"run_in_background":{"type":"boolean","description":"Return the job ID at once"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"edit","description":"Edit a single file using exact text replacement. Every edits[].oldText must match a unique, non-overlapping region of the original file. If two changes affect the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead of emitting overlapping edits. Do not include large unchanged regions just to connect distant changes.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","edits"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to edit (relative or absolute)"},"edits":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["oldText","newText"],"properties":{"oldText":{"type":"string","description":"Exact text for one targeted replacement. It must be unique in the original file and must not overlap with any other edits[].oldText in the same call."},"newText":{"type":"string","description":"Replacement text for this targeted edit."}}},"description":"One or more targeted replacements. Each edit is matched against the original file, not incrementally. Do not include overlapping or nested edits. If two changes touch the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead."}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"write","description":"Write content to a file. Creates the file if it doesn't exist, overwrites if it does. Automatically creates parent directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","content"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to write (relative or absolute)"},"content":{"type":"string","description":"Content to write to the file"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"ask_user","description":"Ask the user 1-4 questions in a panel. Use it instead of listing choices in chat whenever you need a decision, preference or confirmation. Every question also takes a typed answer or a skip. Put a recommended option first and end its label with (Recommended). Returns a line per question: `header: labels`, `header: \"typed\"` or `header: skipped`, then `note: ...` if given; `cancelled` if declined.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["questions"],"properties":{"questions":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":4,"description":"Asked together, one tab each","items":{"type":"object","required":["question","header"],"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"question":{"type":"string","description":"The full question with its context"},"header":{"type":"string","description":"Tab label","maxLength":12},"options":{"type":"array","minItems":2,"maxItems":4,"description":"Omit for a free-text question","items":{"type":"object","required":["label"],"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"label":{"type":"string","description":"Short choice"},"description":{"type":"string","description":"One line"}}}},"multiSelect":{"type":"boolean","description":"Allow several choices"}}}}}}},{"name":"jobs","description":"List, wait on or stop your background jobs. wait returns when the job ends or after timeout seconds (default 30, 10-3600), with its status and last lines; the job keeps running if the wait ends first. stop kills the job and its children.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["action"],"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"action":{"type":"string","enum":["list","wait","stop"]},"id":{"type":"string","description":"For wait and stop"},"timeout":{"type":"number","description":"wait only"}}}},{"name":"monitor","description":"Run a watch command in the background. Each batch of stdout lines it prints reaches you as a notice while you work, so filter it to the events you need (e.g. `tail -f app.log | grep --line-buffered ERROR`). Lines are cut at 500 characters. A monitor that prints too often is rate-limited, then stopped. It ends when the command exits or after timeout seconds. Stderr goes to a separate log.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["command","description"],"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"command":{"type":"string","description":"Watch command; each stdout line is an event"},"description":{"type":"string","description":"Short name shown on its notices"},"timeout":{"type":"number","description":"Seconds, default 300, max 1800 (600 without UI)"}}}},{"name":"get_quotas","description":"Remaining subscription quota per AI provider, from QuotaBar.app. Returns one line per provider: percent or balance left per bucket, plus status and reset time for unhealthy buckets.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"provider":{"type":"string","description":"Provider id, e.g. claude, codex, cursor. Omit for all."}}}},{"name":"subagent_spawn","description":"Start a subagent: a background copy of you with the same instructions and tools, and a fresh context unless forked. Returns its id at once; its full result arrives later as a notice, so end your turn to wait. Pick the cheapest model and thinking level that can do the task.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["description","prompt","model","thinking","isolation"],"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"description":{"type":"string","description":"3-5 word label"},"prompt":{"type":"string","description":"The whole task; unless forked, the child has only this"},"model":{"type":"string","enum":["opencode-go/muse-spark-1.3-contributor","opencode-go/glm-5.3-flash","opencode-go/glm-5.3","opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash","openai/gpt-6-astra","openai/gpt-6-luna","openai/gpt-6.1-sol","openai/gpt-6.1-terra"]},"thinking":{"type":"string","enum":["off","minimal","low","medium","high","xhigh","max"]},"isolation":{"type":"string","enum":["none","worktree"],"description":"worktree: its own git worktree on a new branch, kept if it leaves changes"},"fork":{"type":"boolean","description":"Start from a copy of this conversation"}}}},{"name":"subagent_message","description":"Message one of your subagents. A running one reads it after its current step; a finished one resumes from its saved session and sends a new notice; a queued one gets it added to its prompt. Answer NEEDS_CONTEXT here.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["id","message"],"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"Subagent id"},"message":{"type":"string","description":"What to tell it"}}}},{"name":"subagent_stop","description":"Stop any agent below you: one of your subagents or one of theirs. Every agent under it stops too. Its notice carries its partial output, marked incomplete.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["id"],"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"Subagent id"}}}},{"name":"todo_write","description":"Replace your whole todo list. Use it to plan and track multi-step work, sending the full list on every call.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"todos":{"type":"array","description":"The full list, in order; it replaces the previous one. [] clears it.","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"text":{"type":"string","description":"The task, in a few words."},"status":{"type":"string","enum":["pending","in_progress","completed"],"description":"in_progress when you start the item; completed as soon as it is done."}},"required":["text","status"]}}},"required":["todos"]}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Your instructions are in your system prompt. Begin."}],"timestamp":1794371339524},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_4fb3f931b8b440168c4f02c21f82b105|fc_0b7d58aeb0fd489e016af3ef0d183c87d0b5056ac9f99e317d","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"printf 'first tool done\n'","timeout":30,"run_in_background":false}}],"api":"openai-responses","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-6-luna","usage":{"input":6919,"output":34,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":6953,"cost":{"input":0.0006919000000000001,"output":0.000017,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0007089,"totalFromProvider":false}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794371339543,"responseId":"resp_0b7d58aeb0fd489e016af3ef0c56d087d09fb045099b311750","rawStopReason":"completed","durationMs":2082,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_4fb3f931b8b440168c4f02c21f82b105|fc_0b7d58aeb0fd489e016af3ef0d183c87d0b5056ac9f99e317d","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"first tool done\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":19,"timestamp":1794371341651},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The required first tool call is done.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0b7d58aeb0fd489e016af3ef0ed56887d0ba4f3ae1522947a4\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-responses","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-6-luna","usage":{"input":184,"output":12,"cacheRead":6784,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":6980,"cost":{"input":0.0000184,"output":0.000006,"cacheRead":0.00006784,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00009224,"totalFromProvider":false}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1794371341653,"responseId":"resp_0b7d58aeb0fd489e016a